  "_id": "6a7f5797757ee51246381c60",
  "lab": "6a7f5796eda1a5feaff0b458",
  "name": "Hepatitis Core Antibody IgM (Anti HBc - IgM)",
  "code": "ANTI HBC",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div>Anti-HBc Test Result</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>Positive (Anti-HBc IgM and Anti-HBc IgG)</div></td><td><div>A positive result for both Anti-HBc IgM and Anti-HBc IgG indicates a current or past HBV infection. The presence of Anti-HBc IgM suggests an acute or recent infection, while the presence of Anti-HBc IgG indicates either a past resolved infection or a chronic HBV carrier state. Further testing, including HBsAg and HBV DNA tests, may be needed to determine the stage of the infection and the individual's HBV status.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Negative</div></td><td><div>A negative result for both Anti-HBc IgM and Anti-HBc IgG indicates no previous exposure to HBV. The individual is susceptible to HBV infection and should consider vaccination, especially if they are at risk of exposure to the virus.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
